From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Launcher3 Go: all apps open and close with a swipe, in one step

Launcher3 8.1 opens all apps with a pull-up: a caret floats above the hotseat,
the panel follows the finger, and a gradient at the bottom of the home screen
hints at it. On e-paper every frame of that is a panel update (134 ms at the
fastest, 463 ms with grey), so the panel trails the finger with half-drawn
frames, a half pull leaves all apps half open, and the gradient shows as bands.

The user wants all apps by swiping up, with no hint shown (Test V39: the
navigation bar's all-apps button, asked for in Test V37, made its four
buttons too small, and the bar is back to three). With
FeatureFlags.ALL_APPS_FOLLOW_FINGER false (Launcher3 Go):

  * a vertical swipe on the home screen is detected as before, but nothing
    moves while the finger does; when it lifts, all apps open if the swipe
    went up (a fling's direction, else the finger's travel), and nothing
    happens if it came back down. At the top of the list a swipe down closes
    all apps the same way. Back and home close them too;
  * the transition is the one after a pull; with animations off (frameworks/
    base 0002) it is drawn once, one panel update each way;
  * no caret, no discovery bounce (it is only a redraw without a pull), and no
    gradient on the home screen; behind all apps the ground is plain white.

